ll,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"Hi,\n\nI have project that uses these two plugins at the same time. As I just checked out the project and `npm install`'ed, I could not get the extracted `css` files.\n\nThrough `console.log` around [extract-text line 190](https://github.com/webpack/extract-text-webpack-plugin/blob/master/index.js#L190), I noticed that the extracted modules for the entry points that where not producing css files were empty. The failing entry points where only those going through the `CommonChunk` plugin. The current version last `webpack` [commit](https://github.com/webpack/webpack/commit/779dbd4930a5e54fe6a88b06cef4b153b1d8b7c6) is about this plugin: `support library with CommonsChunkPlugin`.\n\nI force my `webpack` version to `1.4.13` and everything went back to normal.\n\nHere is a very small [project](https://github.com/ArnaudRinquin/webpack-issue-642-replication) that will allow you to replicate the bug (I included the compiled file so you can see what and what's not compiled when running `webpack`).\n\nMy webpack config might be wrong but it used to work.\n\nAny idea how to fix either my config or the `CommonChunkPlugin`?\n","closed_by":{"login":"sokra","id":1365881,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzNjU4ODE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1365881?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sokra","html_url":"https://github.com/sokra","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sokra/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sokra/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sokra/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sokra/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sokra/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sokra/orgs","repos_url":